Subject: [PATCH] ctrl: a policy ACK configures every radio of the agent

em_config sends the Multi-AP Policy Config Request once per agent, from its
first radio; the agent's other radios wait in set_policy_pending. The ACK
moved only the sending radio to configured, so the others never left the
step (and never ran channel selection, scan or topology publish).

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/src/em/policy_cfg/em_policy_cfg.cpp
+++ b/src/em/policy_cfg/em_policy_cfg.cpp
@@ -980,6 +980,17 @@
 		    break;
 	    }
     }
+    // The policy is the agent's: em_config sends it once, from the agent's
+    // first radio, and the others wait in the same step. The ACK configures
+    // them too, or they stay in set_policy_pending.
+    if (match_found) {
+        for (auto &em : em_radios) {
+            if (em->get_state() == em_state_ctrl_set_policy_pending) {
+                em->m_policy_req_msg_id = 0;
+                em->set_state(em_state_ctrl_configured);
+            }
+        }
+    }
     
     if (!match_found) {
 	    em_printfout("No radio waiting for policy config ack for given msg_id");
